  "notes": {
    "a-title": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -420,
      "text": "Concept A · Control room",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 3430,
      "page": "con-a"
    },
    "a-thesis": {
      "x": 3510,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 440,
      "page": "con-a",
      "fill": "gray",
      "text": "Thesis: people who handle a lot of work want a dense, dark, keyboard-fast console where every state reads at a glance.\n\nBest for heavy daily use. Feels technical for occasional users; dark is harder in bright offices.\n\nBuilt from: REF-01 Linear activity trail, REF-02 Linear cards with counts, REF-04 Temporal lanes and recovery, REF-05 Inngest status table, REF-06 n8n nodes.\n\nSections: SEC-nav, SEC-floor, SEC-queues, SEC-list · SEC-header, SEC-facts, SEC-stations, SEC-agent, SEC-decision · SEC-ask, SEC-detail, SEC-actions"
    },
    "b-title": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -420,
      "text": "Concept B · Studio ledger",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 3430,
      "page": "con-b"
    },
    "b-thesis": {
      "x": 3510,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 440,
      "page": "con-b",
      "fill": "gray",
      "text": "Thesis: PSL is a design studio, so its factory should read like a calm, well-set document anyone can pick up without training.\n\nBest for clarity and first impressions, including leadership. Shows fewer items at once.\n\nBuilt from: REF-03 Linear isometric line art, REF-07 Railway mood and view switch, REF-08 Mercury split invoice counts, REF-12 Attio calm light shell.\n\nSections: SEC-nav, SEC-floor, SEC-queues, SEC-list · SEC-header, SEC-facts, SEC-stations, SEC-agent, SEC-decision · SEC-ask, SEC-detail, SEC-actions"
    },
    "m-title": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "text": "Department mascots",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 1440,
      "page": "mascots"
    },
    "m-note": {
      "x": 1520,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "mascots",
      "fill": "orange",
      "text": "Master reference, locked 12 Nov 2026: every later pose must match this image (design/mascots/family-master.png).\n\nStill to come: names, pose sheets (idle, working, waiting for you, done, can't do that), transparent PNGs, avatar crops.\n\nMascots are the department agents. People keep their own avatars, so agent work never looks like a person's decision."
    },
    "d-title": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -420,
      "text": "Concept D · Linear-style",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 3430,
      "page": "con-d"
    },
    "d-thesis": {
      "x": 3510,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 440,
      "page": "con-d",
      "fill": "purple",
      "text": "Thesis: work feels like a fast, quiet issue tracker. Linear's patterns (lists grouped by state, a progress circle per item, properties at the side, activity feed, ⌘K), rebuilt with PSL's own colour and content.\n\nThe progress circle fills as stations complete; orange means it needs you.\n\nBest for people used to modern work tools. Close to concept A in feel, and it borrows another product's conventions instead of a PSL identity.\n\nBuilt from: REF-01 Linear issue detail and activity, REF-02 Linear grouped cards and counts, REF-03 Linear line drawings.\n\nSame sections as A to C."
    },
    "c-title": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -420,
      "text": "Concept C · Assembly line",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 3430,
      "page": "con-c"
    },
    "c-thesis": {
      "x": 3510,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 440,
      "page": "con-c",
      "fill": "orange",
      "text": "Recommended. Thesis: the stations are the product, so every screen leads with the line a piece of work travels and the separate facts it has earned.\n\nBest for understanding where work is and why it is held. Bold structure; the track takes space on small phones.\n\nBuilt from: REF-04 Temporal lanes and recovery, REF-06 n8n nodes and joins, REF-09 Ramp agent filling fields, REF-11 Devin step ticks.\n\nSections: SEC-nav, SEC-floor, SEC-queues, SEC-list · SEC-header, SEC-facts, SEC-stations, SEC-agent, SEC-decision · SEC-ask, SEC-detail, SEC-actions"
    },
    "j02-title": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "text": "J-02 · An approver acts on a decision from an alert",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 2270,
      "page": "j02"
    },
    "j02-note": {
      "x": 2350,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "j02",
      "fill": "gray",
      "text": "Click through with Play: alert → sign in → decision → approved. The last board shows the state when a newer version arrives while you are reading.\n\nDrawn on sample data before architecture (early start, 12 Nov). Alert wording must become a Meta-approved WhatsApp template; no amounts or client details in the message."
    },
    "j01-title": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "text": "J-01 · A PM starts work and follows it to verified",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 6000,
      "page": "j01"
    },
    "j01-note": {
      "x": 2930,
      "y": 1400,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "j01",
      "fill": "gray",
      "text": "Top row, desktop in journey order: queue → start work → work item → verified outputs. Bottom row: the empty queue and the phone versions.\n\nSample data, drawn before architecture (early start, 12 Nov)."
    },
    "j05-title": {
